{"name":"Johannesburg","slug":"johannesburg","region":"Africa","lat":-26.2,"lon":28.05,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Johannesburg has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.4 °C in all. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding Sep–Nov, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 45% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 2 times a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 58 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this warm would come about once every 51 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1.6 °C, against 0.8 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days, and this year's shift is substantial. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1.6 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a drier-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 60%), and a less humid season than normal is likely (about 80% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":19.9958,"trend_per_decade":0.1914,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.4352,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.5055,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.4355,"intrinsic_sd":0.5394,"effect_this_season":1.1121,"effect_ratio":2.0615,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":51.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.5638,"p_below":0.0013,"p_near":0.0126,"p_above":0.9861,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":58.1115,"values":[19.617,20.108,19.578,20.236,18.179,18.336,18.507,19.481,18.987,18.865,19.326,19.748,19.119,20.213,19.084,20.255,19.141,19.446,20.899,19.385,19.024,19.218,20.742,18.669,18.566,17.956,19.547,19.29,19.714,19.02,19.333,19.661,21.038,20.129,20.167,19.556,20.205,20.46,18.195,19.035,20.115,20.493,20.346,18.988,20.073,18.614,19.635,19.843,19.528,18.586,19.321,19.283,20.063,20.427,19.905,19.502,20.844,19.26,19.997,20.116,19.444,20.288,20.244,20.344,20.478,22.187,20.206,20.442,21.114,20.186,20.189,19.309,19.825,20.821,21.176],"forecast_mean":21.5596,"forecast_sd":0.5913,"fit":{"a2027":20.4476,"b":0.5055,"c":0.0191,"tercile_low":19.7736,"tercile_high":20.2588},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1469,"trend_p":0.0005,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3635,"enso_p":0.0008,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.7997,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1905,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.4868,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":1.0709,"lines_cross":