iño, a Mar–May this warm would come about once every 7 years. Mar–May rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a modest but consistent effect toward a drier season, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Mar–May, and this year's shift is substantial. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 85% chance), about 1.3 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a less humid season than normal is likely (about 70% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":15.5414,"trend_per_decade":0.1899,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.424,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3753,"enso_p":0.0001,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.1821,"intrinsic_sd":0.7454,"effect_this_season":0.8257,"effect_ratio":1.1076,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Substantial","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":7.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.3183,"p_below":0.0246,"p_near":0.1282,"p_above":0.8472,"forecast_words":"Likely (85%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":43.4856,"values":[15.053,14.889,15.316,16.908,13.809,15.539,15.033,15.747,15.131,14.028,15.283,15.062,14.36,15.756,15.018,14.975,14.229,13.564,14.736,15.798,15.327,14.328,15.109,13.831,14.028,14.113,14.444,14.468,15.991,15.081,14.562,14.605,16.192,15.604,15.222,16.147,16.767,15.41,14.857,14.76,15.026,16.22,15.419,15.298,14.95,14.451,13.43,16.386,16.243,14.284,15.392,15.835,16.534,15.207,15.244,13.733,16.197,14.502,15.118,16.064,15.431,15.783,15.726,15.369,16.927,16.816,16.023,16.241,17.042,15.351,16.191,15.111,16.302,17.728,15.574],"forecast_mean":16.8597,"forecast_sd":0.8037,"fit":{"a2027":16.034,"b":0.3753,"c":0.019,"tercile_low":15.2796,"tercile_high":16.0364},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_p